  "notes_for_reviewer": "Official SGH fee pages read 2026-10-27: \"Table of fees for undergraduate studies\" (academic year 2026/2027; international students; full-time English-taught EUR 2,500 per semester paid at once, EUR 2,550 in five instalments) and \"Fees for graduate studies\" (2026-2027, EUR per semester; EUR 2,400 per semester paid at once, EUR 2,450 in five instalments; EUR 3,100 / 3,150 for Finance and Accounting with ACCA). The single-payment amount is stored. The master's page does not label the fees as international-student fees explicitly; they are stored as international because the programmes are taught in English. The list of English-taught programmes comes from the SGH page \"etr-easy-read\" (bachelor: four fields; master: five on that page); the master's programmes stored are the five that have a 2026/27 price on the fee page. Management, Entrepreneurship, Technology and Innovation is on the fee page but not on the easy-read page; \"International Master Program in Management Accounting\" is on the easy-read page but not on the fee page and is not stored. The four English-taught bachelor fields are priced by the single row \"Full-time, English-taught\" of the undergraduate table (it does not name the fields). Application fee: PLN 100 if admission includes an entrance exam and PLN 85 otherwise (undergraduate page); the higher value is stored for bachelor programmes. The master's fee page lists none, so none is stored. Durations, intakes and deadlines are not on these pages. Part-time Polish-taught programmes are not stored. ISCED-F codes are inferred from the names (a guess, to review). The suffix (BSc/MSc) in the names is added from the level."
